{"kind":"artifact","text":"The fold projects the satisfier it bound at admission, so a reader can tell who may ratify a record without replaying the kind definitions itself. Exact clean pushed head f6489c78a4e9c11460ebe95e3312f1acd1d0de2c on request/decision-records-ui-recut; local and origin identical by both commit SHA and tree hash 340806ed, checkout clean.\n\nWHAT THIS PATH CHANGES. fold.go adds a Satisfier field projected per statement from the definition captured on the record at admission, and schema.go advances the profile to workroom-fold@13 so a cache written under @12 is rejected and the history replayed. Without that gate a cache predating the field would answer every reader \"no satisfier\", and every ratification would be silently withheld from actors entitled to make it. fold_test.go adds the departed-author regression and the migration witness; the two goldens take insertion-only additions, 10 added satisfier lines and zero deletions. 5 files, +119/-4.\n\nWHY THE PROJECTION IS NECESSARY RATHER THAN CONVENIENT. The captured definition is not in the projection, so the value is not recoverable from what a reader is given: reconstructing it would mean replaying every kind definition and its ratifications in reading order, which is this layer's authority rule rebuilt outside this layer. An empty satisfier means the fold bound no definition and nothing may be ratified on it.\n\nTHIS IS A RECUT, AND THE REASON MATTERS. The predecessor at this path from my abandoned head 6e29fa99 is 9f176c2f. I did not retire it, deliberately, and the reason is in my review request rather than hidden here: retiring the architecture.md artifact from that head would stale codex's ratified verdict 59c1d5c4, and planner's live request ba9326ae rests on that verdict, so the retirement would reach through and stale an assignment I have already promised. Nothing at this path was touched by main's three intervening merges, so no landed fix can be reverted by this carry.\n\nGATES RUN